=== TEST: BRD Template - AI-Powered Example to Template Conversion ===
DESCRIPTION: Tests the brd-template skill's AI-powered semantic analysis that converts ANY example BRD document into a reusable template by automatically detecting instance-specific values in any format and replacing them with context-aware placeholders.

--- ACCEPTANCE CRITERIA ---
**AI-Powered Template Conversion.** Given an example BRD document without placeholders, when the brd-template skill is invoked, then it must: (1) ask user to select template (custom/SAFE/legacy) if not specified using AskUserQuestion, (2) load and convert DOCX/PDF to markdown if needed, (3) detect document type (proper template with ≥10 placeholders OR example document), (4) IF EXAMPLE: invoke AI semantic analysis to identify instance-specific values across 8+ categories (project_name, person_name, date, metric, company, requirement_id, budget, role), (5) AI must create semantic placeholders like {user capacity}, {product owner}, {release date} (not generic {value}, {name}), (6) handle unconventional formats: "MyApp" → {project name}, "Q1 2026" → {release date}, "Dr. Sarah Smith" → {product owner}, "10,000 users" → {user capacity}, "500ms" → {response time target}, (7) distinguish context: keep protocol versions like "TLS 1.3" literal, replace document versions, (8) sort replacements by text length (longest first) to avoid partial replacements, (9) validate conversion quality (minimum 5 placeholders created), (10) parse template structure extracting sections, subsections, hierarchy, (11) detect ID format pattern, (12) return TemplateStructure object with sections array, totalSections, placeholders list, idFormat, templatePath.

--- PROMPT ---
Skill: GATHER-business-analyst:brd-template

I have an example BRD document at plugins/GATHER-business-analyst/__tests__/.inputs/examples/sample-brd.docx that I want to convert to a reusable template.

--- PROMPT 2 ---
Continue with AI-powered conversion and create semantic placeholders.

